From 7beec9601b7d3c80f8d1d01ac209cfaa7e612c87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sixfaced Fixes <fixes@local>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 15:33:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(player): scale down vidfast chrome; fix(keys): register
 Wyzie IPC handlers

Player chrome (MoviePage, TVPage, new utils/playerChromeScript.js):
vidfast renders an oversized title card and centre play button over the
video. Tag those nodes structurally (overlay next to <video>, first
text-only child, largest button, icon buttons) and style them via
data-sb-* attributes. Class selectors are unusable because the provider
uses MUI emotion hashes that change every build. Re-applied on dom-ready
and a few timed passes; idempotent and a no-op if the markup changes.

Wyzie key flow (src/ipc/subtitles.js):
preload.js exposed wyzie-validate-key / wyzie-open-redeem and
WyzieKeyModal called them, but no handler was registered, so the modal
could only show 'No handler registered'. Validate now probes the
authenticated search endpoint; redeem opens the store page in a child
window and watches page text + clipboard for a 'wyzie-' token.
